+### Bounded structured-matmul frontend v4
+
+`StructuredMatmulV4` is private compiler analysis, not a new public operator,
+compiler facade, or wire type. It emits entry `pypto_structured_matmul_v4` and
+metadata schema 4. It accepts one Opaque function with exactly two distinct
+exact `In` parameters, one direct registered `tensor.matmul` assignment, and
+one direct return of that assignment. Both inputs must be plain, fully static,
+contiguous BF16 tensors of the same rank, either rank two or rank three. Rank-3
+batch extents must match exactly; broadcasting is rejected. The result is a
+plain contiguous BF16 tensor with the exact logical `[M,N]` or `[B,M,N]`
+shape. The first bounded shape policy additionally requires `K` to be a
+multiple of 128 and `N` to be a multiple of 16.
+
+Keyword arguments may be absent. If present, the only accepted values are
+exact BF16 `out_dtype`, boolean `a_trans`/`b_trans`, and
+`c_matrix_nz=false`; duplicates, unknown keys, wrong types, and wrong values
+are rejected. Attributes, `tensor.matmul_acc`, mixed dtype/rank, batch
+broadcast, dynamic extents, MemRef/TensorView metadata, nested calls, operand
+reordering, mutation, and extra statements are rejected.
+
+Transpose flags do not become TensorIR matmul attributes. The canonical source
+emits an explicit `transpose` view on the physical dense argument with
+permutation `[1,0]` for rank two or `[0,2,1]` for rank three. It then emits
+BF16-by-BF16 TensorIR `matmul` with an FP32 result and a nearest-even TensorIR
+`convert` from FP32 to the BF16 HIR result. Frontend projections and the
+producer ABI retain the original physical input shapes and dense strides.
+
+For the normalized extents `S` above, preparation requires exactly `len(S)`
+power-of-two tiles no larger than their extents. With
+`r=min(128, lowbit(K))`, it rejects `product(tile)*r > 16,777,216`,
+`ceil(K/r) > INT32_MAX`, or a grid product outside signed-int32 or target
+limits. Finalization requires exactly two input descriptors followed by
+`Result0`, three pointer arguments, output-descriptor-two static grid
+selection, exact tiles and grid, pointer-only packing, and zero workspace.
+
+This source/compiler layer establishes bounded HIR acceptance, deterministic
+TensorIR and frontend identities, and producer ABI checks. It does not claim a
+successful TensorIR/CUDA Tile build for every accepted case, GPU numerical
+correctness, CUDA launch, or performance until separate CPU/compiler and
+real-SM120 gates run. V1/V2/V3 canonical source, projection bytes, callable ABI,
+and producer behavior remain unchanged.
+
